.TH KYTHOS-HELP 1 "2027" "KythOS Kernal" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
kythos-help \- inspect installed commands and their local documentation
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B kythos-help
.RI command " [arguments]"
.br
.B kythos-help
.RI "words describing a command"
.SH DESCRIPTION
Read the local command index to describe an installed executable, its documented
options, and recognized command declarations. Search description words when a
command name is not supplied.
The inspected executable is never run and typed text is not sent to a service.
.PP
In the default interactive Bash configuration, F1 shows help for the current
line while preserving that line. Bash builtins use Bash's own usage text.
User aliases and functions retain their own completion and execution behavior.
.PP
Tab requests a recognized typo or phrase suggestion. A second Tab or Right
Arrow copies a pending suggestion to the line. Ordinary Enter executes it.
Native shell completion remains available when no suggestion applies.
.SH INDEX
The system index is generated from installed executables and packaged manual
pages and refreshed after package transactions. Newly installed executables
are discovered from PATH without a manually maintained command-name list.
Commands without packaged documentation remain usable through the shell;
the helper reports the absence of metadata instead of inventing options.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
kythos-help systemctl
kythos-help list processes
kythos-help tar
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR bash (1),
.BR man (1),
.BR cy (8)
